            <ArticleTitle>[Paravertebral and intra-abdominal abscess due to oxygen-ozone therapy for lower back pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.recot.2013.06.003</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1888-4415(13)00097-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Complications secondary to oxygen-ozone therapy are rare, but they have been described in medical literature. There are only two cases of infectious complications after oxygen-ozone therapy. Our aim is to describe a rare case of purulent complication that was secondary to oxygen-ozone therapy for the treatment of lower back pain. We report the clinical improvement with conservative treatment for a local complication after percutaneous oxygen-ozone treatment. According to the clinical improvement of our patient, conservative treatment should be considered before any aggressive surgery.</AbstractText>
